1
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:16,280
There's so many of them, huh?

2
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,581
Yeah, there are.

3
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,550
I know, right?

4
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:20,756
It's like this pretty much every day.

5
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:23,860
By the way, is Yui feeling any better?

6
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:26,977
Well, she got a good night's
sleep, so I think she's okay.

7
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:28,589
I don't know, you tell me.

8
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,277
Has this ever happened to her before?

9
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,480
We have no idea.

10
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:36,900
You see, we found her on floor
22, wandering in the forest.

11
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,720
The poor thing.

12
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,260
She's lost her memory. Oh.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,824
That's the reason we came here.

14
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:50,157
We thought maybe someone in the town
of Beginnings might know who she is.

15
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:51,070
You live here.

16
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:52,925
Have you ever seen her before?

17
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:54,880
Sorry, I haven't.

18
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:58,904
I mean, there are a lot of kids
in town, but I've never seen her.

19
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:03,857
When the game started, a lot of the children
suffered severe psychological trauma.

20
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:05,937
I couldn't stand by and do nothing,

21
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:10,020
so I moved to this church and made
it a safe place for them to live.

22
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:13,437
I walk through the town every
day looking for kids like these,

23
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:14,797
kids who might need my help?

24
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:17,762
but in all this time, I've
never seen her before.

25
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,500
Back to square one.

26
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,740
Sorry to bother you. I'm Yulier.

27
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,917
And you're with the army, right?

28
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,797
I hope you're not here to start
trouble because of yesterday.

29
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:32,710
God, no.

30
00:01:32,793 --> 00:01:34,497
In fact, I'm here to thank you.

31
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:37,521
You did right by putting
those men in their place.

32
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:42,232
Actually, I came here to ask
the two of you for your help.

33
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:43,310
Seriously?

34
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,269
I can't remember the past,

35
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:03,597
but I can't understand the past.

36
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:08,380
I'm afraid of the past, but
I'm still afraid of the past.

37
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:16,377
I'm still afraid

38
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:19,620
of the sky.

39
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:31,020
Oh

40
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:53,540
and I'm still here, but I'm here to play.

41
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:56,580
I know.

42
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:02,917
It's time for me.

43
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,137
I'll be fine.

44
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,050
I'll be fine.

45
00:03:05,133 --> 00:03:05,963
I'll be fine.

46
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:09,730
Bye.

47
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:11,420
Bye.

48
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,377
When the guild was formed, we...

49
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:24,120
well, actually, it was
our leader, Thinker.

50
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,897
He never wanted it to turn into the kind
of dictatorial organization it's become.

51
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:32,617
At first, the mission of the guild
was to share information and food,

52
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:35,037
equally, among as many
players as possible.

53
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:37,717
But then the guild grew
too large, didn't it?

54
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:38,630
Right.

55
00:03:38,713 --> 00:03:41,717
And after much infighting,
one man became very powerful.

56
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,980
His name is Gabe.

57
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:46,957
Gabe and his group became
stronger and stronger,

58
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:49,537
monopolizing all the best
monster spawn points.

59
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:51,208
They're out of control now,

60
00:03:51,620 --> 00:03:55,267
extorting other players under
the pretext of collecting taxes.

61
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:58,237
It was obvious Gabe didn't
care about clearing the game,

62
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:00,157
and that made a lot of people mad.

63
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,537
He had to do something to get
back in their good graces,

64
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:06,326
so he sent the highest level
players he had to the front lines.

65
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,250
Korvats.

66
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:15,378
Gabe was denounced after
spearheading that massacre.

67
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:19,837
That's when we started to seriously consider
kicking him out of the guild for good.

68
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:24,744
And now that he's scared and getting
desperate, he's decided to eliminate Thinker.

69
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:30,180
He set a trap and stranded
Thinker deep inside a dungeon.

70
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:32,400
Can't he teleport out?

71
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:35,071
Does he have any weapons?

72
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:37,601
He didn't take anything with him.

73
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:40,411
Gibao told him he wanted to talk, unarmed.

74
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,977
Thinker believed him.

75
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,500
That was three days ago.

76
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:45,291
He's been gone that long?

77
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:46,777
Can't he find his way out?

78
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:49,537
The dungeon is the highest
level we've seen so far.

79
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,796
He can't get out of there on his own.

80
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:55,239
As his second-in-command,
this is my responsibility.

81
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:59,800
But the problem is, my level
isn't high enough to reach him.

82
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:05,028
And Gabe is using his influence to keep
the rest of the army from helping me.

83
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:08,637
When I heard that two of the most powerful
players anyone's seen were in town,

84
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:10,357
I thought, this is my chance!

85
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:13,028
I tracked you down
because I need your help.

86
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:14,860
Kirito, Asuna,

87
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:19,620
I beg you, for thinker's sake, Please
help me rescue him from that dungeon.

88
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:26,071
If you think we can help get Thinker
out of there, we'd be glad to help you.

89
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:30,577
However, well, the thing is, we'd like
to make sure you're telling the truth.

90
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:31,490
I'm sorry.

91
00:05:31,573 --> 00:05:33,657
I know we just met and
I'm asking a lot from you.

92
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:39,840
But when I think about him trapped alone
in there, I feel like I'm going insane.

93
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,720
It's okay, Mommy.

94
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:51,580
Everything she's been telling you is
the truth Y-Yui, you mean you can tell?

95
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:56,840
I don't know how I know
she is, but she is.

96
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:08,345
If anything, I'd rather trust her and
regret it than not trust her and regret it?

97
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:11,458
Let's go, it'll all work out, right?

98
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,500
Whatever you say, Mr.

99
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:16,470
Easygoing.

100
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,500
Okay, we'll help.

101
00:06:18,660 --> 00:06:21,072
I just hope we're strong enough to do it.

102
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,520
Thank you so much.

103
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:26,837
I know what it feels like
to want to save someone.

104
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,802
Especially someone you care for.

105
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:32,220
Stay here and wait for us, okay? No!

106
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:33,400
I'm coming too!

107
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:34,860
Oh, come on, Yui.

108
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,697
Don't you want to stay here with me?

109
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:37,610
No!

110
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:39,150
Great.

111
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:41,177
Now we get to see your rebellious side.

112
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:42,277
Hey, this is serious.

113
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:45,831
It's too dangerous for you to
come along with us this time.

114
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,480
I'm going too!

115
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:56,300
I never knew this dungeon was under
the Town of Beginnings. I know.

116
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:59,817
There wasn't anything like
this during the beta test.

117
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:04,017
I think the dungeon opens up to reveal
more as the floors above are cleared.

118
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:07,747
I bet Gabe was planning on
keeping this place all to himself.

119
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:10,567
Exclusive access to
spawns can be profitable.

120
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:14,560
The thing is, the monsters here
are usually around level 60.

121
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:17,234
He wouldn't be able to do much hunting.

122
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:21,135
This is the entrance.

123
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:26,407
Don't worry, I'm not afraid.

124
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:28,000
No, it's okay.

125
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:31,417
Believe it or not, she's a heck
of a lot tougher than she looks.

126
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:33,794
She'll make a fine Swordsman someday.

127
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,716
We should get going.

128
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:01,604
I feel like I should apologize.

129
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,357
He's doing all the fighting.

130
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,120
Oh no, he's happy out there.

131
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,614
Really, he loves getting his battle on.

132
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:12,029
We're pretty far down,
are we almost there?

133
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:16,157
Thinker hasn't moved from
this position for a while now.

134
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:18,860
It could be a safe zone, but I'm not sure.

135
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:22,854
If we can reach it, maybe we
can use a teleport crystal.

136
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,517
Man, I fought my butt off!

137
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,697
I should have helped you.

138
00:08:26,780 --> 00:08:28,757
No, not at all, I had a blast.

139
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,577
Besides, they dropped some items.

140
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:31,490
Really?

141
00:08:31,573 --> 00:08:32,834
You get anything good?

142
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,050
Uh-huh

143
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,330
Huh?

144
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:38,640
What is that?

145
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:40,217
It's scavenged toad meat.

146
00:08:40,300 --> 00:08:41,535
You mean those frogs?

147
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:43,797
Hey, the weirder the meat,
the better the taste.

148
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:45,517
Maybe you can cook it up later.

149
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,718
Not on your flight!

150
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:49,520
What the hell?

151
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:51,978
Oh, come on, what'd you do that for?

152
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:53,860
Damn it. Okay, fine.

153
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,465
What am I gonna do with these?

154
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,210
No!

155
00:08:58,293 --> 00:08:59,760
No, no, no! Asuna!

156
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:01,630
Good meat!

157
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,360
But it's delicious!

158
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:04,697
You just have to pull this one.

159
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:05,610
Here, smile!

160
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:10,274
I've never, ever seen you smile before!

161
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:22,160
Come on, let's go.

162
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:36,440
Look, it's a safe zone.

163
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:40,380
There's a player inside.

164
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,580
It's Thinker!

165
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:43,960
Wait, don't!

166
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,110
Yulier!

167
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,030
Thinker!

168
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:57,220
No, stay away!

169
00:09:57,660 --> 00:09:59,120
The corridor's rigged!

170
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:02,800
Stop! Stop!

171
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,940
Wait, Yulier! Come back!

172
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:23,177
Yulier, take her to the safe
zone and wait for us there, okay?

173
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:24,090
Uh, okay.

174
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:26,800
Mommy! Come on.

175
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:51,814
Asuna, use a teleport crystal and get
Yui and the others out of here now.

176
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,260
I can't see its data with my ID skill.

177
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:57,917
It could be as strong
as something from 490.

178
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,260
I can buy you time.

179
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:00,657
Just get everyone out of here.

180
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:02,237
No way am I leaving you here.

181
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:04,060
I'll catch up! Move it!

182
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,300
Take care of Yui!

183
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:13,457
Run while you still have a chance!

184
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:16,080
Asuna! No! We can't leave! Hurry!

185
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:52,490
Kirito!

186
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:55,060
Yuri, no! It's dangerous! Come back!

187
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:09,280
What are you doing?
Get away from it! Huey!

188
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:15,580
Daddy, Mommy, it's okay.

189
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,240
Huey!

190
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:26,640
An immortal object.

191
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,960
I don't know.

192
00:13:03,940 --> 00:13:09,340
Oh, my God.

193
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:35,180
Uh… Yui?

194
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,797
Yui…

195
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,457
Daddy…

196
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:40,217
Mommy…

197
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,760
Don't worry, I remember everything.

198
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,240
Yui, say something.

199
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:52,091
You remember who you are?

200
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:53,460
Yes.

201
00:13:55,820 --> 00:13:58,040
Kirito, Asuna…

202
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:04,100
Everything in the world of Sword Art
Online is controlled by a single,

203
00:14:04,280 --> 00:14:05,500
massive system.

204
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:08,840
The system is called Cardinal.

205
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:14,067
It was designed to operate entirely on
its own, without any human intervention.

206
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:19,007
Its function is to regulate the balance
of SAO according to its own discretion.

207
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:22,740
From monsters and NPC AI,

208
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:24,997
to drop rates for items and money,

209
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:30,080
Everything here is controlled by the
processes the Cardinal Program executes.

210
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:33,960
That includes the psychological
care of the players.

211
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:39,197
Mental Health Counseling
Program Prototype 1.

212
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:40,380
Codename Yui.

213
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:43,040
That is who I am.

214
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,177
You're a program?

215
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,160
An AI?

216
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:51,197
I was designed to put
players at ease with me.

217
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:54,986
That's why I was given the ability
to emulate complex emotions.

218
00:14:55,680 --> 00:15:00,240
Nothing about me is real
nothing not even my tears.

219
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:02,440
I'm so sorry.

220
00:15:09,820 --> 00:15:14,500
But then what about your amnesia
can that even happen to an AI?

221
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:17,140
Two years ago,

222
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:21,678
on the day of the official launch,
and for reasons I never understood,

223
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:26,355
the Cardinal program banned me from
interacting with any of the players.

224
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:28,780
I wasn't allowed to assist them.

225
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:33,258
I couldn't do anything except continue
monitoring their mental states.

226
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:37,440
Their situation, in a word, was horrible.

227
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,260
No, don't!

228
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:50,037
Terror. Despair. Rage.

229
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:52,557
People were overcome by negative feelings.

230
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:54,460
Some of them couldn't take it.

231
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:55,920
They went insane.

232
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:01,220
Under normal circumstances,

233
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:04,257
my function would have been to
go to such players immediately,

234
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:07,060
but I wasn't permitted
any contact with them.

235
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:14,140
Little by little, errors began piling
up inside of me, and I fell apart.

236
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:21,577
Then, one day, I saw two players.

237
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:24,657
Their mental parameters
were vastly different

238
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:27,093
from anything I'd seen among the others.

239
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:34,100
There was joy, and peace,
and there was something more.

240
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:40,097
I wandered through the playing field,

241
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:43,057
hoping to get as close to
both of you as I could,

242
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:44,493
without being detected.

243
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:47,695
So, that's why you were in the forest?

244
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:49,600
Yes, that's why.

245
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:54,434
I've wanted to meet the two
of you for the longest time.

246
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,371
That's strange, isn't it?

247
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:59,933
It should be impossible for
me to think things like that.

248
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:03,100
I'm not human, I'm a program after all.

249
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:09,255
Yui, maybe what you're feeling
are real human emotions.

250
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:12,980
I don't know.

251
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:14,297
I'm confused.

252
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:15,556
Nothing makes sense.

253
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:17,799
I don't know what's happened to me.

254
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:23,276
You aren't just some program anymore.

255
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,206
The system can't control you.

256
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:29,129
Listen, if you want something,
all you have to do is say it.

257
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:31,602
Go ahead, tell us what you want.

258
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:35,760
What I want.

259
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:39,000
I want.

260
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:45,340
I want to stay with you forever.

261
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:47,660
Daddy!

262
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:49,050
Mommy!

263
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,460
You will.

264
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,980
We'll be together forever, Yui.

265
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:01,440
Yeah.

266
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:04,061
Yeah, remember, you're our child.

267
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,280
It's too late.

268
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:13,680
For what?

269
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:16,330
Look,

270
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:21,500
this is actually a console the GM can use
to gain emergency access to the system.

271
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:26,580
I used it to delete the
monster in the corridor.

272
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:31,880
And now, because I disobeyed
the Cardinal's directive,

273
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:35,100
the system is running
a check on my program.

274
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:37,519
It thinks I'm a foreign object now.

275
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:40,780
I'll probably be deleted at once.

276
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:42,660
Oh no!

277
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,921
There's gotta be a way around it!

278
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:48,320
Daddy, Mommy, thank you.

279
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:50,720
This is goodbye.

280
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:55,930
No!

281
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,660
I don't want that!

282
00:18:58,100 --> 00:18:59,057
Stay with us!

283
00:18:59,140 --> 00:19:00,120
Please stay!

284
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:03,040
We just started living like a real family!

285
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,540
Yui, don't go!

286
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:11,613
Whenever the two of you are around,
you have a way of making people smile.

287
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:17,200
From now on, and for me,
please continue my work.

288
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:18,956
Keep helping people.

289
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:23,900
Share your happiness with all
of them. I can't. I won't.

290
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:25,600
You have to stay with us.

291
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,860
I can't be happy without you.

292
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:33,860
Smile, Mommy.

293
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,820
Cardinal! No! Kayaba!

294
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:10,138
You're gonna find out things don't
always go the way you want them to!

295
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:13,977
Kiriko, where are you?

296
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:18,825
If I'm fast enough, I might be able to
use the GM's account to access the system.

297
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,480
Are you okay?

298
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:39,670
What's this?

299
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:43,575
The system was about to reject
Yui's admin credentials.

300
00:20:44,060 --> 00:20:48,648
The only thing I could do was take her
program and turn it into a game object.

301
00:20:49,460 --> 00:20:51,197
So, this is…

302
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:53,880
You're holding Yui's heart.

303
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,420
Hey, Kirito.

304
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:13,600
If the game does get
cleared, and this world ends…

305
00:21:14,060 --> 00:21:15,825
What's going to happen to Yui?

306
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:17,550
Don't worry.

307
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:22,113
I fixed it so her data will be saved
to the local memory on my nerve gear.

308
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:26,800
When we get back, recreating her the
way she was isn't going to be easy.

309
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:30,580
But if there's a way, we'll find it.

310
00:21:37,340 --> 00:21:38,170
Okay.

311
00:21:38,253 --> 00:21:39,917
As long as we can be a family again.

312
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,097
We'll see her when we get back.

313
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:43,977
Our first child.

314
00:21:44,060 --> 00:21:46,977
Yeah, we'll see her again!

315
00:21:47,060 --> 00:21:49,037
Hey, Asuna.

316
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:50,360
You okay?

317
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:03,180
Good luck, Mommy

318
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:23,160
Thank you.

319
00:23:35,940 --> 00:23:38,480
Next time, Edge of Hell's Abyss.

320
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:40,090
Thank you.
